.\" EROFF.RF - a tour of EROFF: EROFF EROFF.RF > EROFF.TXT, then elfprint -p EROFF.TXT on the Mac
.he 'LTOS 0.5'EROFF'Page %'
.fo ''- % -''
.ll 64
.ce 2
THE ELF2K TEXT FORMATTER
a small nroff for LTOS
.sp 2
.pp
EROFF takes plain text and makes pages of it. Words are gathered into
lines of the length you choose, and the right margin is made straight
by spreading the spaces, the way a typewriter never could.
Requests are lines that begin with a full stop.
.pp
A blank line ends a paragraph, too.

So does a line that starts with spaces:
   this one keeps its indent.
.sp
.in 8
.ti -4
1.  An indented list item, with its number hanging out in the margin
by four columns. The rest of the item lines up under the text.
.ti -4
2.  A second item.
.in 0
.sp
.nf
No fill:   these lines
           come out exactly
           as they were typed.
.fi
.sp
.na
This paragraph is ragged right: .na turns justifying off, and .ad turns it
back on. Long words like antidisestablishmentarianism still wrap cleanly.
.ad
.bp
.ce
SECOND PAGE
.sp
.ll 40
A narrower measure: forty characters a line, set with .ll, makes a column
like a newspaper's.
.bp
.ll 64
.nh Fonts and headings
.pp
Words can be \fBbold\fR or \fIitalic\fR: in the file they are marked, and
elfprint on the Mac prints them in real bold and italic. On the Elf2K's
screen they show plain.
.nh 2 Lists
.ip * 3
A bullet, hanging in the margin; the item's lines line up after it.
.ip * 3
Another bullet.
.ip "(a)" 5
A tag of more than one character.
.lp
A paragraph with no indent ends the list.
.nh 2 Displays
.ds
.B "A display:"
  lines exactly as typed,
  kept together on one page.
.de
.sh Units
.lp
\&.sp takes inches, centimetres, points or lines: .sp 1i is six lines.
.sp 1i
.tl 'left'centre'right'
